    "insights.subPage.explainer.activeEnergyBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die aktive Energie sind die Kalorien, die du durch Bewegung verbrennst, zusätzlich zum Grundumsatz in Ruhe. Sie ist ein direktes Maß dafür, wie körperlich aktiv dein Tag war."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Active energy is the calories you burn through movement, on top of the baseline your body uses at rest. It is a direct measure of how physically active your day was."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "활동 에너지는 몸이 쉬는 동안 쓰는 기초 에너지에 더해, 움직이면서 소모하는 칼로리예요. 하루를 얼마나 활동적으로 보냈는지 직접 보여주는 지표예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.activeEnergyTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aktive Energie"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Active energy"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "활동 에너지"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.audioEventsBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Laute Geräuschereignisse markieren Momente, in denen der Lärm um dich herum ein Niveau erreicht hat, das bei ausreichender Belastung das Gehör schädigen kann. Häufige Ereignisse sind ein Hinweis, eine ruhigere Umgebung oder Gehörschutz zu suchen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Loud sound events flag moments when noise around you reached a level that can harm hearing with enough exposure. Frequent events are a cue to seek quieter surroundings or hearing protection."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "큰 소리 노출은 주변 소음이 충분히 오래 노출되면 청력을 해칠 수 있는 수준에 이른 순간을 표시해요. 자주 발생한다면 더 조용한 곳을 찾거나 청력 보호 장비를 쓰라는 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.audioEventsTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Laute Geräuschereignisse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Loud sound events"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "큰 소리 노출"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bloodGlucoseBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Blutzucker ist die Zuckermenge in deinem Blut, die wichtigste Energiequelle des Körpers. Er steigt nach dem Essen und pendelt sich zwischen den Mahlzeiten ein; dauerhaft hohe Werte können auf Diabetes oder Prädiabetes hinweisen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blood glucose is the amount of sugar in your blood, the body's main energy source. It rises after eating and settles between meals; readings that stay high over time can signal diabetes or prediabetes."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈당은 혈액 속 당의 양으로, 몸의 주요 에너지원이에요. 식사 후 올라갔다가 식사 사이에 안정돼요. 수치가 계속 높게 유지되면 당뇨병이나 당뇨병 전단계의 신호일 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bloodGlucoseTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blutzucker"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blood glucose"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈당"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bloodPressureBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Blutdruck ist die Kraft, die das Blut auf die Gefäßwände ausübt, angegeben als systolisch zu diastolisch (Spitzenwert beim Herzschlag über dem Ruhewert dazwischen). Dauerhaft hohe Werte belasten Herz und Gefäße auf Dauer."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blood pressure is the force your blood exerts on the artery walls, written as systolic over diastolic (the peak during a heartbeat over the resting value between beats). Consistently high readings strain the heart and blood vessels over time."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈압은 혈액이 동맥 벽에 가하는 힘으로, 수축기/이완기(심장이 뛸 때의 최고값/박동 사이 휴식기의 값)로 표시해요. 수치가 계속 높으면 시간이 지나면서 심장과 혈관에 부담을 줘요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bloodPressureTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blutdruck"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Blood pressure"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈압"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bmiBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der BMI ist dein Gewicht geteilt durch deine Körpergröße zum Quadrat und ordnet dich einer groben Gewichtskategorie zu. Er unterscheidet nicht zwischen Muskeln und Fett."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "BMI is your weight divided by your height squared, giving a single number that places you in a broad weight category. It does not distinguish muscle from fat."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "BMI는 체중을 키의 제곱으로 나눈 값으로, 대략적인 체중 범주를 하나의 숫자로 보여줘요. 근육과 지방을 구분하지는 못해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bmiTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Body-Mass-Index (BMI)"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Body mass index (BMI)"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체질량지수(BMI)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bodyTemperatureBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Körpertemperatur spiegelt deinen Kernwärmezustand wider, normalerweise um 37 °C mit kleinen Tagesschwankungen. Ein anhaltender Anstieg kann auf eine Infektion hindeuten; nächtliche Messungen am Handgelenk erfassen vor allem relative Änderungen, keinen klinischen Wert."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Body temperature reflects your core thermal state, normally around 37 °C with small daily swings. A sustained rise can indicate infection, while overnight wrist readings mainly track relative changes rather than a clinical value."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체온은 몸 중심부의 온도 상태를 나타내며, 보통 37 °C 안팎에서 하루 중 조금씩 오르내려요. 체온이 계속 높으면 감염의 신호일 수 있고, 밤사이 손목에서 측정한 값은 임상적인 수치보다는 주로 상대적인 변화를 보여줘요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bodyTemperatureTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Körpertemperatur"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Body temperature"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체온"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bodyWaterBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Das Gesamtkörperwasser ist der Anteil deines Körpergewichts, der aus Flüssigkeit in und um die Zellen besteht. Es schwankt mit Flüssigkeitshaushalt, Ernährung und Aktivität, daher sagt der Trend über Wochen mehr aus als ein einzelner Wert."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Total body water is the share of your body weight made up of fluid, inside and around your cells. It shifts with hydration, food, and activity, so the trend over weeks tells you more than any single reading."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체수분은 체중 가운데 세포 안팎의 수분이 차지하는 비율이에요. 수분 섭취, 음식, 활동에 따라 달라지므로 한 번의 측정값보다 몇 주에 걸친 추세가 더 많은 것을 알려줘요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.bodyWaterTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gesamtkörperwasser"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Total body water"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체수분"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.boneMassBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Knochenmasse ist das geschätzte Gewicht der Mineralien in deinem Skelett. Waagengestützte Schätzungen sind ungefähr, doch ein gleichbleibender oder steigender Trend unterstützt die langfristige Knochenstärke."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bone mass is the estimated weight of the mineral in your skeleton. Scale-based estimates are approximate, but a steady or rising trend supports long-term bone strength."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "골량은 골격에 있는 무기질의 추정 무게예요. 체중계로 추정한 값은 근사치이지만, 유지되거나 늘어나는 추세는 장기적인 뼈 건강에 도움이 돼요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.boneMassTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Knochenmasse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bone mass"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "골량"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.breathingDisturbancesBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Deine Apple Watch kann schätzen, wie oft deine Atmung im Schlaf unterbrochen war. Ein niedriger Index ist besser; die Einstufung als erhöht stammt von Apple, nicht von HealthLog."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Your Apple Watch can estimate how often your breathing was interrupted during sleep. A lower index is better; the elevated classification comes from Apple, not from HealthLog."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apple Watch는 수면 중 호흡이 얼마나 자주 중단됐는지 추정할 수 있어요. 지수가 낮을수록 좋아요. 높음 분류는 HealthLog가 아니라 Apple이 정한 것이에요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.breathingDisturbancesTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Atemaussetzer im Schlaf"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sleep breathing disturbances"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "수면 중 호흡 장애"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.cardioFitnessBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "VO₂max gibt an, wie viel Sauerstoff dein Körper bei maximaler Anstrengung verwerten kann. Es ist der aussagekräftigste Laborwert für die Ausdauerfitness; ein höherer oder steigender Wert spricht für eine gute Herz-Kreislauf-Gesundheit."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "VO₂ max is how much oxygen your body can use at peak effort. It is the single best lab marker of aerobic fitness, and a higher or rising value is a strong sign of cardiovascular health."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "VO₂ max는 최대로 힘을 낼 때 몸이 사용할 수 있는 산소량이에요. 유산소 체력을 보여주는 가장 좋은 단일 검사 지표이고, 값이 높거나 올라가고 있다면 심혈관 건강의 강력한 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.cardioFitnessTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cardiofitness (VO₂max)"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cardio fitness (VO₂ max)"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "심폐 체력 (VO₂ max)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.cardioRecoveryBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Erholungspuls gibt an, um wie viele Schläge pro Minute dein Puls in der ersten Minute nach dem Ende einer anstrengenden Belastung fällt. Ein größerer Abfall bedeutet, dass sich dein Herz schneller beruhigt. Das ist ein Zeichen guter Fitness."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cardio recovery is how many beats per minute your heart rate falls in the first minute after you stop hard exercise. A bigger drop means your heart settles down faster, which is a sign of good fitness."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "심박 회복은 강도 높은 운동을 멈춘 뒤 첫 1분 동안 심박수가 분당 몇 회 떨어지는지예요. 많이 떨어질수록 심장이 더 빨리 안정된다는 뜻이고, 이는 체력이 좋다는 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.cardioRecoveryTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Erholungspuls"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cardio recovery"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "심박 회복"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.daylightBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Zeit im Tageslicht ist, wie lange du dich täglich im Freien im Licht aufhältst. Regelmäßiges Tageslicht unterstützt einen gesunden Schlaf-Wach-Rhythmus und die Stimmung, und Zeit im Freien ist mit der Augengesundheit verbunden."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Time in daylight is how long you spend in outdoor light each day. Regular daylight supports a healthy sleep-wake rhythm and mood, and time outdoors is linked to eye health."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "햇빛 노출 시간은 하루 동안 야외의 빛 아래에서 보낸 시간이에요. 꾸준히 햇빛을 쬐면 건강한 수면-각성 리듬과 기분에 도움이 되고, 야외 활동 시간은 눈 건강과도 관련이 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.daylightTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Zeit im Tageslicht"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Time in daylight"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "햇빛 노출 시간"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.doubleSupportTimeBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Doppelunterstützungszeit ist der Anteil jedes Gehzyklus, in dem beide Füße gleichzeitig den Boden berühren. Ein höherer Prozentsatz bedeutet meist ein vorsichtigeres, weniger stabiles Gangbild."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Double support time is the share of each walking cycle when both feet touch the ground at once. A higher percentage usually means a more cautious, less stable gait."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "양발 지지 시간은 한 걸음 주기 가운데 두 발이 동시에 땅에 닿아 있는 시간의 비율이에요. 비율이 높으면 대개 더 조심스럽고 덜 안정적인 걸음걸이를 뜻해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.doubleSupportTimeTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Doppelunterstützungszeit"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Double support time"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "양발 지지 시간"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.environmentalAudioBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Umgebungslautstärke erfasst die Lautstärke deiner Umwelt in Dezibel. Anhaltende Belastung über etwa 70 dB kann das Gehör mit der Zeit schädigen, daher sind niedrigere Tagesmittel sicherer."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Environmental sound levels track the loudness of the world around you in decibels. Prolonged exposure above about 70 dB can damage hearing over time, so lower daily averages are safer."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "환경 소음은 주변 소리의 크기를 데시벨로 나타내요. 약 70 dB 이상의 소음에 오래 노출되면 시간이 지나면서 청력이 손상될 수 있어서, 하루 평균이 낮을수록 안전해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.environmentalAudioTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Umgebungslautstärke"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Environmental sound levels"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "환경 소음 수준"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fallsBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hier werden die von deiner Apple Watch erkannten schweren Stürze gezählt. Null ist das Ziel; eine steigende Zahl ist ein Hinweis auf ein erhöhtes Sturzrisiko."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This counts the hard falls your Apple Watch detects. Zero is the goal; a rising count is a mobility-risk signal."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apple Watch가 감지한 심한 넘어짐 횟수예요. 0이 목표예요. 횟수가 늘어나면 이동 능력 관련 위험 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fallsTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Stürze"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Falls"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "낙상"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fatFreeMassBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die fettfreie Masse ist alles in deinem Körper, das kein Fett ist: Muskeln, Knochen, Organe und Wasser. Sie zu halten oder aufzubauen, während das Gewicht sinkt, deutet meist auf eine gesündere Körperzusammensetzung hin."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fat-free mass is everything in your body that is not fat: muscle, bone, organs, and water. Holding or building it while losing weight usually signals healthier body composition."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "제지방량은 몸에서 지방을 뺀 모든 것, 즉 근육, 뼈, 장기, 수분이에요. 체중을 줄이면서 이를 유지하거나 늘리면 대개 체성분이 더 건강해지고 있다는 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fatFreeMassTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fettfreie Masse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fat-free mass"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "제지방량"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fatMassBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Fettmasse ist das Gesamtgewicht des Körperfetts. Etwas Fett ist für Hormone und Energiespeicher unverzichtbar, doch zu viel (besonders am Bauch) erhöht das langfristige Gesundheitsrisiko."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fat mass is the total weight of fat in your body. Some fat is essential for hormones and energy storage, but too much, especially around the abdomen, raises long-term health risk."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체지방량은 몸에 있는 지방의 총 무게예요. 어느 정도의 지방은 호르몬과 에너지 저장에 꼭 필요하지만, 특히 복부에 지방이 너무 많으면 장기적인 건강 위험이 커져요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.fatMassTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fettmasse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Fat mass"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체지방량"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.flightsClimbedBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die gestiegenen Etagen zählen die Stockwerke, die du täglich nach oben gehst, wobei eine Etage etwa drei Metern Höhe entspricht. Es ist ein einfacher Marker für Alltagsaktivität und Beinarbeit."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Flights climbed counts the floors you go up each day, with one flight roughly ten feet of elevation. It is a simple marker of incidental activity and lower-body effort."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "오른 층수는 하루 동안 올라간 층 수예요. 한 층은 약 10피트 높이예요. 일상 속 활동량과 하체 운동량을 간단히 보여주는 지표예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.flightsClimbedTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Etagen gestiegen"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Flights climbed"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "오른 층수"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.headphoneAudioBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Kopfhörerlautstärke erfasst in Dezibel, wie laut du über Ohrhörer oder Kopfhörer hörst. Die Lautstärke niedrig zu halten und Pausen einzulegen schützt dein Gehör langfristig."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Headphone audio levels track how loudly you listen through earbuds or headphones, in decibels. Keeping the volume down and taking breaks protects your hearing over the long run."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "헤드폰 음량은 이어폰이나 헤드폰으로 듣는 소리의 크기를 데시벨로 나타내요. 볼륨을 낮추고 중간중간 쉬면 장기적으로 청력을 보호할 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.headphoneAudioTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Kopfhörerlautstärke"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Headphone audio levels"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "헤드폰 음량 수준"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.hrvBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die HRV ist die kleine Schwankung der Zeit zwischen aufeinanderfolgenden Herzschlägen. Eine höhere Variabilität spiegelt meist ein gut erholtes, anpassungsfähiges Nervensystem wider, ein anhaltender Rückgang kann auf Erschöpfung, Stress oder mangelnde Erholung hinweisen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "HRV is the tiny variation in time between consecutive heartbeats. Higher variability usually reflects a well-recovered, adaptable nervous system, while a sustained drop can signal fatigue, stress, or insufficient recovery."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "HRV는 연속된 심장 박동 사이 간격의 미세한 변화예요. 변이도가 높으면 대개 잘 회복되고 적응력 있는 신경계를 반영하고, 계속 떨어지면 피로, 스트레스, 회복 부족의 신호일 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.hrvTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Herzfrequenzvariabilität (HRV)"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Heart rate variability (HRV)"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "심박변이도 (HRV)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.leanBodyMassBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Magermasse ist dein Gesamtgewicht abzüglich des Körperfetts, also Muskeln, Knochen, Organe und Wasser zusammen. Sie neben dem Gewicht zu verfolgen zeigt, ob Veränderungen aus Muskeln oder aus Fett stammen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Lean body mass is your total weight minus body fat, meaning muscle, bone, organs, and water combined. Tracking it alongside weight shows whether changes come from muscle or from fat."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "제지방 체중은 전체 체중에서 체지방을 뺀 값으로, 근육, 뼈, 장기, 수분을 합친 무게예요. 체중과 함께 기록하면 변화가 근육에서 왔는지 지방에서 왔는지 알 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.leanBodyMassTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Magermasse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Lean body mass"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "제지방 체중"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.medicationsBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Therapietreue zeigt, wie zuverlässig du deine Medikamente wie verordnet einnimmst, hier als Anteil der erwarteten Dosen, die du erfasst hast. Eine gleichmäßige Einnahme entscheidet oft darüber, ob eine Therapie wie beabsichtigt wirkt."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Adherence is how reliably you take your medication as prescribed, shown here as the share of expected doses you actually logged. Steady intake is often what makes a treatment work as intended."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "복약 순응도는 처방대로 얼마나 꾸준히 약을 복용하는지를 나타내며, 여기서는 예정된 복용 가운데 실제로 기록한 비율로 보여줘요. 꾸준한 복용이 치료가 의도대로 효과를 내는 데 중요한 경우가 많아요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.medicationsTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Medikamenten-Therapietreue"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Medication adherence"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "복약 순응도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.moodBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Stimmungserfassung hält auf einer einfachen Skala fest, wie du dich fühlst. Regelmäßiges Protokollieren zeigt Muster, die ein einzelner Tag nie offenbart: etwa wie Schlaf, Aktivität oder Medikamente mit dem Befinden zusammenhängen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mood tracking records how you feel over time on a simple scale. Logging it regularly reveals patterns that a single day never shows, like how sleep, activity, or medication line up with how you feel."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "기분 기록은 간단한 척도로 시간에 따른 기분을 남겨요. 꾸준히 기록하면 하루만 봐서는 알 수 없는 패턴, 예를 들어 수면, 활동, 약이 기분과 어떻게 맞물리는지가 드러나요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.moodTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Stimmung"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mood"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "기분"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.muscleMassBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Muskelmasse ist das geschätzte Gewicht der Muskeln in deinem Körper. Mehr Muskeln unterstützen Kraft, Stoffwechsel und Beweglichkeit und müssen mit zunehmendem Alter aktiv erhalten werden."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Muscle mass is the estimated weight of the muscle in your body. More muscle supports strength, metabolism, and mobility, and it tends to need active effort to preserve as you age."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "근육량은 몸에 있는 근육의 추정 무게예요. 근육이 많을수록 근력, 대사, 이동 능력에 도움이 되고, 나이가 들수록 유지하려면 꾸준한 노력이 필요한 편이에요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.muscleMassTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Muskelmasse"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Muscle mass"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "근육량"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.oxygenSaturationBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die SpO₂ ist der Prozentsatz der roten Blutkörperchen, die Sauerstoff transportieren. Werte von 95 bis 100 % sind in Ruhe normal; Werte, die dauerhaft unter 90 % liegen, verdienen Aufmerksamkeit, kurze nächtliche Abfälle sind jedoch häufig."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "SpO₂ is the percentage of your red blood cells carrying oxygen. Readings of 95 to 100% are normal at rest; values that stay below 90% warrant attention, though brief nightly dips are common."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "SpO₂는 산소를 운반하는 적혈구의 비율이에요. 안정 시 95~100%면 정상이고, 계속 90% 미만이면 주의가 필요해요. 다만 밤사이 잠깐 떨어지는 것은 흔해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.oxygenSaturationTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sauerstoffsättigung (SpO₂)"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Oxygen saturation (SpO₂)"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "산소포화도(SpO₂)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.pulseBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Puls gibt an, wie oft das Herz pro Minute schlägt. Eine Einzelmessung spiegelt den Moment wider. In Ruhe liegt er meist bei 60 bis 100 Schlägen pro Minute und steigt natürlicherweise bei Bewegung, Stress oder Koffein."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Your pulse is how many times your heart beats per minute. A spot reading reflects what you were doing in the moment. At rest it is typically 60 to 100 beats per minute, and it rises naturally with movement, stress, or caffeine."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "맥박은 심장이 1분에 뛰는 횟수예요. 한 번 측정한 값은 그 순간 무엇을 하고 있었는지를 반영해요. 안정 시에는 보통 분당 60~100회이고, 움직임, 스트레스, 카페인에 따라 자연스럽게 올라가요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.pulseTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Puls"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pulse"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "맥박"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.pulseWaveVelocityBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Pulswellengeschwindigkeit misst, wie schnell die Druckwelle jedes Herzschlags durch deine Arterien läuft. Eine schnellere Welle weist auf steifere Arterien hin, was mit einem höheren Herz-Kreislauf-Risiko verbunden ist."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pulse wave velocity measures how fast the pressure wave from each heartbeat travels along your arteries. A faster wave indicates stiffer arteries, which is linked to higher cardiovascular risk."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "맥파 속도는 심장이 뛸 때마다 생기는 압력파가 동맥을 따라 얼마나 빠르게 전달되는지 측정해요. 압력파가 빠를수록 동맥이 더 딱딱하다는 뜻이고, 이는 심혈관 위험 증가와 관련이 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.pulseWaveVelocityTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pulswellengeschwindigkeit"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pulse wave velocity"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "맥파 전파 속도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.respiratoryRateBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Atemfrequenz ist die Anzahl der Atemzüge pro Minute. In Ruhe atmen die meisten Erwachsenen etwa zwölf- bis zwanzigmal pro Minute; ein anhaltender Anstieg kann mit Krankheit, Anstrengung oder Stress einhergehen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Respiratory rate is the number of breaths you take per minute. At rest most adults breathe roughly twelve to twenty times a minute; a sustained rise can accompany illness, exertion, or stress."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "호흡수는 1분 동안 숨 쉬는 횟수예요. 안정 시 대부분의 성인은 분당 약 12~20회 호흡해요. 호흡수가 계속 높으면 질병, 신체 활동, 스트레스와 함께 나타날 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.respiratoryRateTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Atemfrequenz"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Respiratory rate"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "호흡수"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.restingHrBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Ruhepuls ist die Herzfrequenz in völliger Ruhe, meist über Nacht gemessen. Ein niedriger Ruhepuls deutet in der Regel auf eine bessere Herz-Kreislauf-Fitness hin, ein steigender Trend kann ein frühes Zeichen für Stress oder Krankheit sein."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Resting heart rate is your heart rate when you are completely at rest, usually measured overnight. A lower resting rate generally points to better cardiovascular fitness, and a rising trend can be an early sign of stress or illness."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "안정 시 심박수는 완전히 쉬고 있을 때의 심박수로, 보통 밤사이에 측정해요. 안정 시 심박수가 낮을수록 대체로 심혈관 체력이 좋다는 뜻이고, 올라가는 추세는 스트레스나 질병의 초기 신호일 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.restingHrTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ruhepuls"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Resting heart rate"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "안정 시 심박수"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.sixMinuteWalkBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dies ist Apples Schätzung, wie weit du in sechs Minuten gehen könntest. Dahinter steht ein etablierter klinischer Test für Mobilität und kardiopulmonale Ausdauer. Eine gleichbleibende oder steigende Strecke ist ein gutes Zeichen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This is Apple's estimate of how far you could walk in six minutes, based on a long-standing clinical test of mobility and cardiopulmonary endurance. A steady or rising distance is a good sign."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Apple이 추정한 6분 동안 걸을 수 있는 거리예요. 이동 능력과 심폐 지구력을 평가하는 오랜 임상 검사를 바탕으로 해요. 거리가 유지되거나 늘어나면 좋은 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.sixMinuteWalkTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "6-Minuten-Gehstrecke"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Six-minute walk distance"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "6분 보행 거리"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.skinTemperatureBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Hauttemperatur ist hier die kleine nächtliche Abweichung deiner Handgelenkstemperatur von deinem eigenen Ausgangswert, keine absolute Fiebermessung. Veränderungen können Schlaf, Umgebung, Krankheit oder Zyklusphase widerspiegeln."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Skin temperature here is the small nightly change in your wrist temperature from your own baseline, not an absolute fever reading. Shifts can track sleep, environment, illness, or menstrual-cycle phase."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "여기서 피부 온도는 내 기준값 대비 밤사이 손목 온도의 작은 변화로, 절대적인 발열 수치가 아니에요. 변화는 수면, 환경, 질병, 생리 주기 단계를 따라 나타날 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.skinTemperatureTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hauttemperatur"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Skin temperature"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "피부 온도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.sleepBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Schlafdauer ist die tatsächlich geschlafene Zeit pro Nacht, aufgeteilt in Leicht-, Tief- und REM-Schlaf. Die meisten Erwachsenen brauchen etwa sieben bis neun Stunden; gleichmäßige Menge und Qualität unterstützen Erholung, Stimmung und Stoffwechsel."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sleep duration is how long you actually slept across the night, split into light, deep, and REM stages. Most adults need roughly seven to nine hours; both consistent quantity and quality support recovery, mood, and metabolism."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "수면 시간은 밤사이 실제로 잠든 시간으로, 얕은 수면, 깊은 수면, REM 수면 단계로 나뉘어요. 대부분의 성인은 약 7~9시간이 필요해요. 꾸준한 수면 시간과 질 모두 회복, 기분, 대사에 도움이 돼요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.sleepTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Schlaf"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sleep"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "수면"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stairAscentSpeedBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dies gibt an, wie schnell du eine Treppe hinaufgehst. Es ist ein empfindlicher Marker für Beinkraft und Mobilität. Ein gleichbleibendes oder steigendes Tempo ist gut, ein sinkendes solltest du im Blick behalten."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This is how fast you climb a flight of stairs. It is a sensitive marker of leg strength and mobility. A steady or rising pace is a good sign, and a falling one is worth watching."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "계단 한 층을 얼마나 빨리 오르는지예요. 다리 근력과 이동 능력을 민감하게 보여주는 지표예요. 속도가 유지되거나 빨라지면 좋은 신호이고, 느려진다면 지켜볼 만해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stairAscentSpeedTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Treppensteig-Tempo"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Stair ascent speed"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "계단 오르기 속도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stairDescentSpeedBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dies gibt an, wie schnell du eine Treppe hinabgehst. Zusammen mit dem Steig-Tempo zeigt es Beinkontrolle und Gleichgewicht. Ein gleichmäßiges Tempo ist gut, ein sinkendes solltest du im Blick behalten."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This is how fast you go down a flight of stairs. Together with ascent speed it tracks leg control and balance. A steady pace is a good sign, and a falling one is worth watching."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "계단 한 층을 얼마나 빨리 내려가는지예요. 오르기 속도와 함께 다리 조절 능력과 균형을 보여줘요. 속도가 유지되면 좋은 신호이고, 느려진다면 지켜볼 만해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stairDescentSpeedTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Treppab-Tempo"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Stair descent speed"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "계단 내려가기 속도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stepLengthBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Schrittlänge ist der durchschnittliche Abstand von einem Fußauftritt zum nächsten. Eine über die Zeit kürzere Schrittlänge kann Müdigkeit, Vorsicht oder eine veränderte Beweglichkeit widerspiegeln."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Step length is the average distance from one footfall to the next. A shorter step over time can reflect fatigue, caution, or a change in mobility."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보폭은 한 발이 땅에 닿은 지점에서 다음 발이 닿는 지점까지의 평균 거리예요. 시간이 지나면서 보폭이 짧아지면 피로, 조심스러움, 또는 이동 능력의 변화를 반영할 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.stepLengthTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Schrittlänge"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Step length"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보폭"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.trigger": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Was ist %@?"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "What is %@?"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@란?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.vascularAgeBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Das Gefäßalter ist die Schätzung deines Geräts, wie alt sich deine Arterien im Vergleich zu deinem tatsächlichen Alter verhalten, ermittelt anhand der Arteriensteifigkeit. Ein Gefäßalter unter dem echten Alter deutet auf gesündere Blutgefäße hin. Deine Waage oder dein Ring hat die Schätzung ermittelt, und sie blickt auf vergangene Werte zurück, statt etwas vorherzusagen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vascular age is your device’s estimate of how old your arteries behave compared with your actual age, based on arterial stiffness. A vascular age below your real age suggests healthier blood vessels. Your scale or ring derived the estimate, and it looks back at past readings rather than predicting anything."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈관 나이는 동맥 경직도를 바탕으로 내 동맥이 실제 나이와 비교해 몇 살처럼 기능하는지 기기가 추정한 값이에요. 혈관 나이가 실제 나이보다 낮으면 혈관이 더 건강하다는 뜻일 수 있어요. 이 추정값은 체중계나 링이 계산한 것으로, 과거 측정값을 되돌아볼 뿐 무언가를 예측하지는 않아요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.vascularAgeTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gefäßalter"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vascular age"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "혈관 나이"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.visceralFatBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Viszeralfett ist das Fett, das tief im Bauchraum um die Organe gespeichert wird. Anders als das Unterhautfett ist ein hoher Wert eng mit Herzkrankheiten und Typ-2-Diabetes verbunden, daher ist niedriger meist besser."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Visceral fat is the fat stored deep in the abdomen around your organs. Unlike fat under the skin, a high level is closely linked to heart disease and type 2 diabetes, so lower is generally better."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "내장지방은 복부 깊숙이 장기 주변에 쌓이는 지방이에요. 피하지방과 달리 수치가 높으면 심장 질환, 제2형 당뇨병과 밀접한 관련이 있어서, 대체로 낮을수록 좋아요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.visceralFatTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Viszeralfett"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Visceral fat"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "내장지방"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingAsymmetryBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Gangasymmetrie ist der Anteil der Zeit, in der deine Schritte zwischen linkem und rechtem Bein ungleichmäßig sind. Ein höherer Prozentsatz kann auf Schmerzen, eine Verletzung oder ein Gangproblem hindeuten, das näher betrachtet werden sollte."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking asymmetry is the share of time your steps are uneven between the left and right leg. A higher percentage can point to pain, injury, or a gait problem worth looking into."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 비대칭은 걸을 때 왼발과 오른발의 걸음이 고르지 않은 시간의 비율이에요. 비율이 높으면 통증, 부상, 또는 살펴볼 만한 보행 문제가 있다는 뜻일 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingAsymmetryTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gangasymmetrie"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking asymmetry"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 비대칭"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingDistanceBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Geh- und Laufstrecke ist die Strecke, die du täglich zu Fuß zurücklegst. Sie ergänzt die Schrittzahl, indem sie zeigt, wie weit du dich bewegt hast, nicht nur wie oft du getreten bist."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking and running distance is the ground you cover on foot each day. It complements step count by reflecting how far you moved, not just how often you stepped."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "걷기 및 달리기 거리는 하루 동안 두 발로 이동한 거리예요. 걸음 수를 보완해서, 얼마나 자주 걸었는지뿐 아니라 얼마나 멀리 움직였는지 보여줘요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingDistanceTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Geh- + Laufstrecke"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking + running distance"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "걷기 + 달리기 거리"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingHeartRateBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Herzfrequenz beim Gehen ist dein durchschnittlicher Puls bei einem gleichmäßigen Spaziergang. Ein über die Zeit niedrigerer Wert spiegelt bei gleicher Anstrengung oft eine bessere Herz-Kreislauf-Fitness wider."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking heart rate is your average pulse during a steady walk. A lower walking rate over time often reflects improving cardiovascular fitness for the same effort."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 심박수는 일정한 속도로 걸을 때의 평균 맥박이에요. 시간이 지나면서 보행 심박수가 낮아지면, 같은 활동에 대한 심혈관 체력이 좋아지고 있다는 뜻인 경우가 많아요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingHeartRateTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Herzfrequenz beim Gehen"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking heart rate"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 심박수"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingSpeedBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Gehgeschwindigkeit ist, wie schnell du dich auf ebenem Untergrund fortbewegst. Sie ist ein gut untersuchter Marker für allgemeine Gesundheit und Beweglichkeit, und ein gleichbleibendes oder steigendes Tempo ist ein gutes Zeichen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking speed is how fast you move on a level walk. It is a well-studied marker of overall health and mobility, and a steady or rising pace is a good sign."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 속도는 평지를 걸을 때 얼마나 빠르게 움직이는지예요. 전반적인 건강과 이동 능력을 보여주는 잘 연구된 지표이고, 속도가 유지되거나 빨라지면 좋은 신호예요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingSpeedTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gehgeschwindigkeit"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking speed"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 속도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingSteadinessBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Gehstabilität schätzt, wie stabil und ausgewogen dein Gangbild ist, eingeteilt von OK bis niedrig. Ein niedriger Wert deutet auf ein höheres Sturzrisiko hin."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking steadiness estimates how stable and balanced your gait is, classed from OK to low. A lower level points to a higher chance of a fall."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 안정성은 걸음걸이가 얼마나 안정적이고 균형 잡혀 있는지 추정해서 양호부터 낮음까지 등급으로 나눠요. 등급이 낮을수록 낙상 가능성이 높다는 뜻이에요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.walkingSteadinessTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gehstabilität"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Walking steadiness"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "보행 안정성"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.weightBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Das Körpergewicht ist eines der einfachsten Signale für die langfristige Energiebilanz und die allgemeine Gesundheit. Der Trend über Wochen zählt weit mehr als ein einzelner Wert, der mit Flüssigkeit, Ernährung und Tageszeit schwankt."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Body weight is one of the simplest signals of long-term energy balance and overall health. The trend over weeks matters far more than any single reading, which fluctuates with hydration, food, and time of day."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체중은 장기적인 에너지 균형과 전반적인 건강을 보여주는 가장 간단한 신호 중 하나예요. 한 번의 측정값은 수분, 음식, 시간대에 따라 오르내리므로 몇 주에 걸친 추세가 훨씬 중요해요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.weightTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gewicht"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Weight"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "체중"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.workoutsBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Workouts sind die strukturierten Trainingseinheiten, die deine Geräte mit Art, Dauer und Energie aufzeichnen. Ihre Erfassung zeigt, wie sich regelmäßiges Training über Wochen summiert und wie es mit deinen anderen Gesundheitssignalen zusammenhängt."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Workouts are the structured exercise sessions your devices record, with type, duration, and energy. Tracking them shows how regular training accumulates over weeks and how it relates to your other health signals."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "운동은 기기가 기록한 체계적인 운동 세션으로, 종류, 시간, 에너지가 함께 기록돼요. 기록해 두면 꾸준한 운동이 몇 주에 걸쳐 어떻게 쌓이는지, 다른 건강 신호와 어떤 관련이 있는지 볼 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.workoutsTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Workouts"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Workouts"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "운동"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.wristTemperatureBody": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Die Handgelenktemperatur wird im Schlaf gemessen. Apple zeigt sie als Abweichung von deinem persönlichen Ausgangswert; ein gleichmäßiger Wert ist normal, ein anhaltender Anstieg kann auf Krankheit, intensives Training oder eine Zyklusveränderung hindeuten."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Wrist temperature is measured while you sleep. Apple shows it as the difference from your personal baseline; a steady reading is normal, while a sustained rise can hint at illness, intense training, or a cycle change."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "손목 온도는 잠자는 동안 측정해요. Apple은 이를 내 개인 기준값과의 차이로 보여줘요. 값이 일정하면 정상이고, 계속 올라가면 질병, 고강도 운동, 생리 주기 변화의 신호일 수 있어요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "insights.subPage.explainer.wristTemperatureTitle": {
      "comment": "Insights — per-metric explainer (mirrors web insights.subPage.explainer)",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Handgelenktemperatur"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Wrist temperature"
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "손목 온도"
          }
        }
      }
    },
